WEBVTT

NOTE Original presentation narration. Phrase timing uses local speech recognition aligned to the production timeline.

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.093
[Soft instrumental music]
Meet Vibe Toxicology LIS:

2
00:00:03.353 --> 00:00:06.273
a free lab system for small toxicology
labs,

3
00:00:06.393 --> 00:00:07.873
on one computer you own.

4
00:00:08.652 --> 00:00:10.472
The day starts with the work queues:

5
00:00:10.672 --> 00:00:13.272
orders to decide, specimens to receive,

6
00:00:13.452 --> 00:00:15.772
results to review, and reports to release.

7
00:00:16.802 --> 00:00:18.742
At the front desk, orders are recorded

8
00:00:18.762 --> 00:00:20.622
exactly as the clinic sent them:

9
00:00:20.882 --> 00:00:24.002
the tests, the diagnoses, and the
medication list.

10
00:00:24.322 --> 00:00:26.302
Nothing is guessed or filled in.

11
00:00:26.642 --> 00:00:28.562
Accepting the order takes one click.

12
00:00:29.598 --> 00:00:32.218
Receiving the specimen creates the
accession,

13
00:00:32.378 --> 00:00:33.858
records when it was collected,

14
00:00:34.138 --> 00:00:36.118
and prints a barcode label for the
container.

15
00:00:40.684 --> 00:00:44.404
On the bench, worklists gather the waiting
specimens for each method.

16
00:00:44.844 --> 00:00:47.424
Every run tracks its calibrators and
controls,

17
00:00:47.784 --> 00:00:50.543
and quality control is assessed for each
analyte.

18
00:00:51.498 --> 00:00:53.638
Results arrive straight from the analyzers

19
00:00:53.658 --> 00:00:56.258
and from mass spectrometry result files.

20
00:00:56.798 --> 00:00:59.718
Anything that doesn't fit is set aside,
with the reason.

21
00:01:00.743 --> 00:01:02.863
Every result is technically reviewed.

22
00:01:03.343 --> 00:01:06.063
Values are shown against the laboratory's
cutoffs,

23
00:01:06.143 --> 00:01:08.843
and each approval records who reviewed it,
and when.

24
00:01:12.550 --> 00:01:15.810
Release rechecks every quality-control and
identity hold

25
00:01:15.830 --> 00:01:17.170
at the moment of release,

26
00:01:17.430 --> 00:01:19.670
and asks for the releaser's password.

27
00:01:20.190 --> 00:01:22.070
The report becomes a versioned record

28
00:01:22.090 --> 00:01:24.271
that corrections never overwrite.

29
00:01:25.244 --> 00:01:27.944
Each delivery is logged with the evidence
it has.

30
00:01:28.164 --> 00:01:29.384
Never just, delivered.

31
00:01:30.665 --> 00:01:33.685
Billable services come from the work
actually performed,

32
00:01:34.045 --> 00:01:35.565
not from positive results.

33
00:01:37.395 --> 00:01:40.255
A tamper-evident audit trail records every
change

34
00:01:40.275 --> 00:01:42.435
and every view of sensitive data,

35
00:01:42.675 --> 00:01:44.495
and can verify its own chain.

36
00:01:45.475 --> 00:01:46.975
And your data stays yours:

37
00:01:47.375 --> 00:01:49.735
encrypted backups to the drives you
choose,

38
00:01:49.975 --> 00:01:53.142
restore tests, and a complete export
whenever you want it.

39
00:01:54.114 --> 00:01:56.034
Vibe Toxicology LIS.

40
00:01:56.054 --> 00:01:58.294
Free, offline-first, and yours.

41
00:01:58.416 --> 00:02:01.233
[Music fades out]
